cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GRBV Transcriptomics Analysis: grapevine red blotch disease and the timing of berry ripening programs"
message: "If this code contributes to published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Prem Pratap
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7921-9379"
    affiliation: "Department of Plant Pathology, University of California, Davis"
repository-code: "https://github.com/prem-p-singh/GRBV-Transcriptomics-Analysis"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - grapevine red blotch virus
  - Vitis vinifera
  - RNA-seq
  - fruit ripening
  - developmental timing
  - Snakemake
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a repeated-measures RNA-seq study of grapevine red blotch
  virus in Merlot berries: 327 libraries from 44 vines across four ripening
  stages and two seasons. A healthy-only developmental reference separates the
  common ripening delay in infected fruit from program-specific timing and
  expression changes. Network, multi-omics, pathway and cross-study analyses
  run as a Snakemake workflow on SLURM; figures are R scripts.
